<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela's Lagoven asphalt sales rise 22 pct.</title>
<headline>Venezuela's Lagoven asphalt sales rise 22 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan state oil subsidiary Lagoven said its asphalt exports hit 32,000 barrels per day (bpd) in 1996, up 22 percent on the previous year.</p>
<p>The company, which is a subsidiary of state-run Petroleos de Venezuela (PDVSA), said it sold more than half its exports to the east coast of the United States, but also found customers in New Zealand, Sweden, Canada and Chile, making it the highest volume asphalt seller in the world.</p>
<p>((--Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
</text>
